    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7-a1">

                <pb facs="0039" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg693"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[A.—Inclosure 1 in No.
                    364.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Excellent to Mr.
                            Bassett.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bueeau of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May 3</hi>,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: It has come to the knowledge of
                    the government that certain rebels, who these last days have resisted its
                    authority in firing upon its troops, and who still resist, have taken refuge,
                    they and their adherents, in the country house which you occupy at Turgean.</p>
                <p>The government desires to know the names of these individuals, who have indeed
                    killed this morning a soldier of one of our posts not far from your house.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, Mr. Minister, to salute you with a very high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>EXCELLENT,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State for
                            Foreign Affairs.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. E. D. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bassett</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister-Resident of the United States, Port au
                            Prince.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
